-- title:
--   Smoothness of the Igusa pole chart over k
-- statement:
--   Fix a level $N \ge 1$ and a prime $\ell$ with $\ell \nmid N$, and let $k$ be an algebraically closed field of characteristic $\ell$. Write $\mathbb{Z}_{(\ell)}$ for the subring [`GaloisRep.ratLocalizedAt ℓ`](def/GaloisRep_Flat.html#L8) of $\mathbb{Q}$ consisting of those rationals whose denominator is coprime to $\ell$, and let $\varphi \colon \mathbb{Z}_{(\ell)} \to k$ be a ring homomorphism. Let `chartAlgInf N ℓ` be the $\mathbb{Z}_{(\ell)}$-subalgebra of the full modular function field of level $N$ formed by the elements integral over the $\mathbb{Z}_{(\ell)}$-subalgebra generated by $j^{-1}$, where $j$ is the modular invariant viewed in that field. The assertion is that the second projection of the fibre product of $\operatorname{Spec}$ of the structure map $\mathbb{Z}_{(\ell)} \to \mathtt{chartAlgInf}\,N\,\ell$ against $\operatorname{Spec}\varphi \colon \operatorname{Spec} k \to \operatorname{Spec}\mathbb{Z}_{(\ell)}$, that is the morphism $\operatorname{Spec}(\mathtt{chartAlgInf}\,N\,\ell) \times_{\operatorname{Spec}\mathbb{Z}_{(\ell)}} \operatorname{Spec} k \to \operatorname{Spec} k$, is smooth of relative dimension $1$.
--
--   This is the pole chart ($j = \infty$) half of the statement that the Igusa model of the modular curve of level $N$ is smooth of relative dimension $1$ over a residue field of characteristic $\ell \nmid N$. It feeds, together with its $j$-finite counterpart, into [`ModularCurve.IgusaScheme.smoothOfRelativeDimension_one_pullback_residue`](thm.html#ModularCurve.IgusaScheme.smoothOfRelativeDimension_one_pullback_residue), the corresponding statement for the scheme obtained by gluing the two charts.
